pssssst GREATEST COMMON DIVISOR
pssssst Euclid's algorithm: gcd(a, b) = gcd(b, a mod b), until b is nothing.
pssssst Horses have moods: run with CLIPCLOP_CALM=1 to see what was supposed to happen.

the SingularHorse gcd ridden by SingularHorse a and SingularHorse b says \
  whinny b \
    snort cl0p says a stomp \
    nicker says giddyup gcd with b and a % b

pssssst gcd(48, 18) = 6
giddyup gcd with cl1pcl1pcl0pcl0pcl0pcl0p and cl1pcl0pcl0pcl1pcl0p

pssssst gcd(17, 5) = 1
giddyup gcd with cl1pcl0pcl0pcl0pcl1p and cl1pcl0pcl1p

pssssst lowest common multiple, from the gcd: lcm(4, 6) = 12
pssssst (there is no precedence, so a * b / gcd really is (a * b) / gcd)
the SingularHorse lcm ridden by SingularHorse a and SingularHorse b says \
  a * b / giddyup gcd with a and b
giddyup lcm with cl1pcl0pcl0p and cl1pcl1pcl0p
